{
  "about": "Invented couple chats for the promise-extraction eval (scripts/eval-promises.mjs). No real people's messages. `line` is the index of the message that holds the promise (a list means any of them is right). `what` lists keywords that must all appear in the extracted phrase (`a|b` = either). `when` lists acceptable times; [] means no time was stated, and \"\" inside a list means an empty time is also fine. `to` is who the promise is owed to (A->B, B->A, both->each other); the extractor implies it from `by`. `optional` items are judgment calls: finding them is not a false positive, missing them is not a miss. `traps` mark lines that look like promises but are not, so false positives can be named.",
